window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b207-9625f9ef987a56f4.json"]={sha256:"9625f9ef987a56f411e63e51ee0121b96805dadc8af7733838594888430a57d5",value:{"id":"b207","title":"錦屏一級水壩","titleEn":"Jinping-I Dam","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"錦屏一級案例從拱座幾何與岩體路徑開始，逐步處理水壓合力、預應力、地震慣性、噴流水舌與熱變形。水庫端再加入季節儲存和取水溫度的守恆，強調結構、消能與生態證據不可互相替代。所有模型保留量綱並列出需要三維分析的缺項。","summaryEn":"The Jinping I case begins with abutment geometry and rock load paths, then addresses water-force resultants, prestress, seismic inertia, spillway jets and thermal movement. Seasonal storage and withdrawal-temperature balances extend the reservoir boundary. Structural, dissipation and ecological evidence cannot substitute for one another, and every dimensional model identifies questions requiring three-dimensional analysis.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["高壩水壓投影","High dam pressure projection"],["雙滑面岩楔抗力","Two plane wedge resistance"],["挑流水舌射程","Ski jump jet travel"],["壩塊自由收縮","Dam block free contraction"],["相關監測聯合殘差","Correlated monitoring residuals"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["高壩水壓投影","雙滑面岩楔抗力","挑流水舌射程","壩塊自由收縮","相關監測聯合殘差"],"labelsEn":["High dam pressure projection","Two plane wedge resistance","Ski jump jet travel","Dam block free contraction","Correlated monitoring residuals"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為本課原創情境串接，所有數值是假設，不能視為業主設計圖或操作許可。先完成「高壩水壓投影」的守恆與邊界檢核，再比較「薄拱圈膜力尺度」及「雙滑面岩楔抗力」的不同控制量。第一組計算為 gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN；第二組為 p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa。學員須保留量綱、資料時間與量測位置，討論誤差如何傳到結果，將第三單元的限制寫入同一張決策表。任何未納入的結構、河道或機組耦合都列為下一階段工作，不由單一得數推論全工程安全。","textEn":"This original sequence connects the first three units using assumed inputs; none is an owner drawing or an operating authorization. First establish conservation and boundaries for High dam pressure projection, then compare the controlling variables in Thin arch ring membrane scale and Two plane wedge resistance. The first calculation is gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN; the second is p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa. Preserve dimensions, observation times, and measurement locations in the working sheet. Explain how input uncertainty changes each conclusion and include the third unit limitations in the same decision table. Structural, river, and machine interactions omitted by a model remain subsequent work; a single numerical answer cannot demonstrate safety of the complete project.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b207-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「高壩水壓投影」與「薄拱圈膜力尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"High dam pressure projection\" and \"Thin arch ring membrane scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b207-v15-01","title":"高壩水壓投影：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"High dam pressure projection: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「高壩水壓投影」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “High dam pressure projection” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直投影積分可得每單位壩長的水平合力，作用點位於壓力三角形形心。這是外力帳，並未說明拱壩如何把力傳向兩岸。實際雙曲面上的法向壓力需向量積分，不能把投影條帶合力直接當成每條拱圈的反力。 合力作用點由壓力一階矩決定，不是幾何深度中點；分段壓力圖改變時，力與力矩都需重新積分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高壩水壓投影」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, and integration over a vertical projection gives horizontal force per unit dam length at the triangular pressure centroid. This accounts for external load, not arch transfer to the banks. Normal pressure on a double-curved surface requires vector integration; a projected strip is not an individual arch reaction. The resultant location follows the first pressure moment, not the geometric midpoint; changing a piecewise pressure diagram requires recalculating both force and moment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “High dam pressure projection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高壩水壓投影」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “High dam pressure projection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-01-k1","title":"高壩水壓投影","titleEn":"High dam pressure projection","text":"靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直投影積分可得每單位壩長的水平合力，作用點位於壓力三角形形心。這是外力帳，並未說明拱壩如何把力傳向兩岸。","textEn":"Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, and integration over a vertical projection gives horizontal force per unit dam length at the triangular pressure centroid. This accounts for external load, not arch transfer to the banks.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高壩水壓投影」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High dam pressure projection\" is correct?","options":["壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深","靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直投影積分可得每單位壩長的水平合力，作用點位於壓力三角形形心。","平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力"],"optionsEn":["Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration.","Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, and integration over a vertical projection gives horizontal force per unit dam length at the triangular pressure centroid.","Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直投影積分可得每單位壩長的水平合力，作用點位於壓力三角形形心。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, and integration over a vertical projection gives horizontal force per unit dam length at the triangular pressure centroid. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b207-v15-02","title":"高壩水壓投影：定量估算","titleEn":"High dam pressure projection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高壩水壓投影」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “High dam pressure projection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN。模型邊界：垂直矩形投影條帶的靜水合力，不含尾水與動水壓。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN. Model boundary: hydrostatic resultant on a vertical rectangular projected strip, excluding tailwater and hydrodynamic pressure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先標出水面與投影面幾何，確認壓力深度不等於海拔高程，再以分層矩形積分接近三角形結果。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark the water surface and projected geometry, ensuring depth is not confused with elevation, then refine rectangular pressure integration toward the triangular result.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN。模型邊界：垂直矩形投影條帶的靜水合力，不含尾水與動水壓。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN. Model boundary: hydrostatic resultant on a vertical rectangular projected strip, excluding tailwater and hydrodynamic pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高壩水壓投影」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High dam pressure projection\", which statement holds?","options":["所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加","所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN。"],"optionsEn":["All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states.","Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: gamma=9.81 kN/m3; h=260 m; w=1 m; F=0.5*gamma*h*h*w=331578 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b207-v15-03","title":"高壩水壓投影：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High dam pressure projection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高壩水壓投影」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “High dam pressure projection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先標出水面與投影面幾何，確認壓力深度不等於海拔高程，再以分層矩形積分接近三角形結果。將外力方向與拱圈傳力圖分開繪製，若兩者合力不平衡，應查漏列尾水或幾何投影。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark the water surface and projected geometry, ensuring depth is not confused with elevation, then refine rectangular pressure integration toward the triangular result. Draw external loading separately from arch transfer. An unbalanced resultant calls for checking omitted tailwater or projection geometry rather than adjusting support reactions arbitrarily. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將水深降低一成，重算合力與作用點並比較非線性變化，再畫出有尾水時的差壓圖，說明哪些力尚未進入投影條帶模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce depth by ten percent, recalculate resultant and location, and compare the nonlinear change. Draw a differential-pressure diagram with tailwater and identify forces still absent from the projected-strip model.","failure":"注意干擾：使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先標出水面與投影面幾何，確認壓力深度不等於海拔高程，再以分層矩形積分接近三角形結果。將外力方向與拱圈傳力圖分開繪製，若兩者合力不平衡，應查漏列尾水或幾何投影。","textEn":"Mark the water surface and projected geometry, ensuring depth is not confused with elevation, then refine rectangular pressure integration toward the triangular result. Draw external loading separately from arch transfer. An unbalanced resultant calls for checking omitted tailwater or projection geometry rather than adjusting support reactions arbitrarily.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將水深降低一成，重算合力與作用點並比較非線性變化，再畫出有尾水時的差壓圖，說明哪些力尚未進入投影條帶模型。","textEn":"Reduce depth by ten percent, recalculate resultant and location, and compare the nonlinear change. Draw a differential-pressure diagram with tailwater and identify forces still absent from the projected-strip model.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高壩水壓投影」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High dam pressure projection\"?","options":["先標出水面與投影面幾何，確認壓力深度不等於海拔高程，再以分層矩形積分接近三角形結果。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失"],"optionsEn":["Mark the water surface and projected geometry, ensuring depth is not confused with elevation, then refine rectangular pressure integration toward the triangular result.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先標出水面與投影面幾何，確認壓力深度不等於海拔高程，再以分層矩形積分接近三角形結果。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark the water surface and projected geometry, ensuring depth is not confused with elevation, then refine rectangular pressure integration toward the triangular result. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b207-v15-04","title":"高壩水壓投影：失效診斷","titleEn":"High dam pressure projection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高壩水壓投影」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “High dam pressure projection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate. Ignoring curved-surface normal components can also omit vertical action, so a horizontal projected-force account does not constitute the complete loading of the dam. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：合力作用點由壓力一階矩決定，不是幾何深度中點；分段壓力圖改變時，力與力矩都需重新積分。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resultant location follows the first pressure moment, not the geometric midpoint; changing a piecewise pressure diagram requires recalculating both force and moment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。","textEn":"Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate. Ignoring curved-surface normal components can also omit vertical action, so a horizontal projected-force account does not constitute the complete loading of the dam.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高壩水壓投影」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High dam pressure projection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。","平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate.","Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b207-v15-05","title":"薄拱圈膜力尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thin arch ring membrane scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「薄拱圈膜力尺度」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thin arch ring membrane scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想圓拱圈在均勻徑向壓力下可藉膜壓縮傳力，壓力乘半徑再除厚度提供一個應力尺度。雙曲拱壩還有豎向懸臂、扭曲及不同剛度拱座，不能當成孤立薄圓環。教材特意保留薄度與荷載假設，讓學員指出何處需要三維殼或實體分析。 膜應力尺度不含外壓失穩與局部缺陷效應，即使材料壓縮強度足夠，也不能由這一式排除所有失效機制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「薄拱圈膜力尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An ideal circular ring under uniform radial pressure carries membrane compression, with pressure times radius divided by thickness giving a stress scale. A double-curvature dam also has vertical cantilever action, distortion and unequal abutment stiffness, unlike an isolated thin ring. State slenderness and loading assumptions before identifying questions requiring shell or solid analysis. The membrane scale omits external-pressure instability and local defects; adequate compressive material strength therefore does not exclude every failure mechanism through this one equation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thin arch ring membrane scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「薄拱圈膜力尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thin arch ring membrane scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-05-k1","title":"薄拱圈膜力尺度","titleEn":"Thin arch ring membrane scale","text":"理想圓拱圈在均勻徑向壓力下可藉膜壓縮傳力，壓力乘半徑再除厚度提供一個應力尺度。雙曲拱壩還有豎向懸臂、扭曲及不同剛度拱座，不能當成孤立薄圓環。","textEn":"An ideal circular ring under uniform radial pressure carries membrane compression, with pressure times radius divided by thickness giving a stress scale. A double-curvature dam also has vertical cantilever action, distortion and unequal abutment stiffness, unlike an isolated thin ring.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「薄拱圈膜力尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thin arch ring membrane scale\" is correct?","options":["平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力","兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分","理想圓拱圈在均勻徑向壓力下可藉膜壓縮傳力，壓力乘半徑再除厚度提供一個應力尺度。"],"optionsEn":["Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible.","Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.","An ideal circular ring under uniform radial pressure carries membrane compression, with pressure times radius divided by thickness giving a stress scale."],"answer":2,"explanation":"理想圓拱圈在均勻徑向壓力下可藉膜壓縮傳力，壓力乘半徑再除厚度提供一個應力尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An ideal circular ring under uniform radial pressure carries membrane compression, with pressure times radius divided by thickness giving a stress scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b207-v15-06","title":"薄拱圈膜力尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Thin arch ring membrane scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「薄拱圈膜力尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thin arch ring membrane scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa。模型邊界：理想薄圓環均勻徑向壓力，R/t=15；僅教學膜壓應力尺度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa. Model boundary: ideal thin circular ring under uniform radial pressure with R/t=15; a teaching membrane-compression scale only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢查半徑與厚度定義及其比例，畫出截開半環的平衡圖，再以粗細網格比較理想模型。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check radius, thickness and their ratio, draw equilibrium of a cut half-ring, and compare mesh refinements of the ideal model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa。模型邊界：理想薄圓環均勻徑向壓力，R/t=15；僅教學膜壓應力尺度。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa. Model boundary: ideal thin circular ring under uniform radial pressure with R/t=15; a teaching membrane-compression scale only.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「薄拱圈膜力尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thin arch ring membrane scale\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa。","理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心","單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa.","The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole.","Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: p=2 MPa; R=180 m; t=12 m; sigma=p*R/t=30 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b207-v15-07","title":"薄拱圈膜力尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thin arch ring membrane scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「薄拱圈膜力尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thin arch ring membrane scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢查半徑與厚度定義及其比例，畫出截開半環的平衡圖，再以粗細網格比較理想模型。若加入不對稱支承後出現彎矩，應承認膜力近似缺項，不用調整半徑把彎曲反應硬塞回公式。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check radius, thickness and their ratio, draw equilibrium of a cut half-ring, and compare mesh refinements of the ideal model. Bending after introducing asymmetric supports identifies a missing mechanism; changing the radius to force agreement does not repair the membrane approximation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將厚度增加兩成重算膜應力，再加入概念性的拱座轉角，指出哪些新內力無法由原式得到，並規劃三維模型需輸入的邊界資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase thickness by twenty percent and recompute membrane stress. Introduce an abutment rotation conceptually, identify internal forces missing from the formula, and list boundary data required for a three-dimensional model.","failure":"注意干擾：拱座變形不相容會引入彎曲與局部拉應力，平均膜壓縮仍可能很大；所以正的平均壓應力不能排除接縫張開，也不能代替混凝土與岩體接觸檢核。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incompatible abutment movement introduces bending and local tension while mean membrane compression remains large. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢查半徑與厚度定義及其比例，畫出截開半環的平衡圖，再以粗細網格比較理想模型。若加入不對稱支承後出現彎矩，應承認膜力近似缺項，不用調整半徑把彎曲反應硬塞回公式。","textEn":"Check radius, thickness and their ratio, draw equilibrium of a cut half-ring, and compare mesh refinements of the ideal model. Bending after introducing asymmetric supports identifies a missing mechanism; changing the radius to force agreement does not repair the membrane approximation.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將厚度增加兩成重算膜應力，再加入概念性的拱座轉角，指出哪些新內力無法由原式得到，並規劃三維模型需輸入的邊界資料。","textEn":"Increase thickness by twenty percent and recompute membrane stress. Introduce an abutment rotation conceptually, identify internal forces missing from the formula, and list boundary data required for a three-dimensional model.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「薄拱圈膜力尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thin arch ring membrane scale\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","檢查半徑與厚度定義及其比例，畫出截開半環的平衡圖，再以粗細網格比較理想模型。","相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check radius, thickness and their ratio, draw equilibrium of a cut half-ring, and compare mesh refinements of the ideal model.","Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head."],"answer":1,"explanation":"檢查半徑與厚度定義及其比例，畫出截開半環的平衡圖，再以粗細網格比較理想模型。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check radius, thickness and their ratio, draw equilibrium of a cut half-ring, and compare mesh refinements of the ideal model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b207-v15-08","title":"薄拱圈膜力尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thin arch ring membrane scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「薄拱圈膜力尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thin arch ring membrane scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"拱座變形不相容會引入彎曲與局部拉應力，平均膜壓縮仍可能很大；所以正的平均壓應力不能排除接縫張開，也不能代替混凝土與岩體接觸檢核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incompatible abutment movement introduces bending and local tension while mean membrane compression remains large. A positive average compressive stress therefore does not exclude joint opening or replace checks of concrete-rock contact and local stress distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：膜應力尺度不含外壓失穩與局部缺陷效應，即使材料壓縮強度足夠，也不能由這一式排除所有失效機制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The membrane scale omits external-pressure instability and local defects; adequate compressive material strength therefore does not exclude every failure mechanism through this one equation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"拱座變形不相容會引入彎曲與局部拉應力，平均膜壓縮仍可能很大；所以正的平均壓應力不能排除接縫張開，也不能代替混凝土與岩體接觸檢核。","textEn":"Incompatible abutment movement introduces bending and local tension while mean membrane compression remains large. A positive average compressive stress therefore does not exclude joint opening or replace checks of concrete-rock contact and local stress distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄拱圈膜力尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thin arch ring membrane scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分","拱座變形不相容會引入彎曲與局部拉應力，平均膜壓縮仍可能很大；所以正的平均壓應力不能排除接縫張開，也不能代替混凝土與岩體接觸檢核。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.","Incompatible abutment movement introduces bending and local tension while mean membrane compression remains large."],"answer":2,"explanation":"拱座變形不相容會引入彎曲與局部拉應力，平均膜壓縮仍可能很大；所以正的平均壓應力不能排除接縫張開，也不能代替混凝土與岩體接觸檢核。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incompatible abutment movement introduces bending and local tension while mean membrane compression remains large. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b207-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「雙滑面岩楔抗力」與「錨索長期力保留」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Two plane wedge resistance\" and \"Long term anchor force retention\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b207-v15-09","title":"雙滑面岩楔抗力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Two plane wedge resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「雙滑面岩楔抗力」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Two plane wedge resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"深谷岩楔可能同時受兩組節理面約束，各面的有效正向力與摩擦係數都會影響可用抗力。教材在已給定法向反力的前提下加總沿假想運動方向的摩擦，避免用單一坡角代表全部三維幾何。真正反力須由向量平衡求得，不能憑重量任意平均分配。 兩面抗力在真實空間須按向量合成，本例同方向相加是額外假設，不能直接轉用到不同交線方位。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙滑面岩楔抗力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A canyon wedge may be constrained by two joint planes, each with its own effective normal force and friction. Given resolved reactions, sum the assumed friction contributions along a movement direction rather than representing all geometry by one slope angle. Actual reactions must follow vector equilibrium, not arbitrary equal division of wedge weight. Resistance contributions require vector combination in real space; adding them along one direction is an extra assumption here and cannot transfer unchanged to other intersection geometries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Two plane wedge resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙滑面岩楔抗力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Two plane wedge resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-09-k1","title":"雙滑面岩楔抗力","titleEn":"Two plane wedge resistance","text":"深谷岩楔可能同時受兩組節理面約束，各面的有效正向力與摩擦係數都會影響可用抗力。教材在已給定法向反力的前提下加總沿假想運動方向的摩擦，避免用單一坡角代表全部三維幾何。","textEn":"A canyon wedge may be constrained by two joint planes, each with its own effective normal force and friction. Given resolved reactions, sum the assumed friction contributions along a movement direction rather than representing all geometry by one slope angle.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙滑面岩楔抗力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Two plane wedge resistance\" is correct?","options":["深谷岩楔可能同時受兩組節理面約束，各面的有效正向力與摩擦係數都會影響可用抗力。","兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分","所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加"],"optionsEn":["A canyon wedge may be constrained by two joint planes, each with its own effective normal force and friction.","Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.","All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states."],"answer":0,"explanation":"深谷岩楔可能同時受兩組節理面約束，各面的有效正向力與摩擦係數都會影響可用抗力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A canyon wedge may be constrained by two joint planes, each with its own effective normal force and friction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b207-v15-10","title":"雙滑面岩楔抗力：定量估算","titleEn":"Two plane wedge resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙滑面岩楔抗力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Two plane wedge resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN。模型邊界：兩面摩擦皆沿同一假想抗滑方向且正向力已知，無黏聚及錨索。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN. Model boundary: both friction contributions act along one assumed resistance direction with known normal forces, no cohesion or anchors. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用立體節理圖先確認共同交線與出露條件，再將每面水壓與反力方向畫出。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use a three-dimensional joint diagram to establish intersection and daylighting, then show pressure and reaction on each plane.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN。模型邊界：兩面摩擦皆沿同一假想抗滑方向且正向力已知，無黏聚及錨索。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN. Model boundary: both friction contributions act along one assumed resistance direction with known normal forces, no cohesion or anchors.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙滑面岩楔抗力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Two plane wedge resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN。","出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失"],"optionsEn":["Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.","Original hypothetical example.","A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: N1=30 MN; U1=6 MN; mu1=0.6 (dimensionless); N2=20 MN; U2=4 MN; mu2=0.5 (dimensionless); R=mu1*(N1-U1)+mu2*(N2-U2)=22.4 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b207-v15-11","title":"雙滑面岩楔抗力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Two plane wedge resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙滑面岩楔抗力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Two plane wedge resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用立體節理圖先確認共同交線與出露條件，再將每面水壓與反力方向畫出。比較乾季和雨季的孔壓變化，若只有一面明顯反應，應保留兩面差異，不用平均水壓抹平主導失效路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use a three-dimensional joint diagram to establish intersection and daylighting, then show pressure and reaction on each plane. Compare seasonal pressures; if one plane responds strongly, retain that distinction rather than averaging pressure and concealing the controlling resistance path. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別提高第一面與第二面水壓，計算抗力變化並比較敏感度，再畫出一面失去接觸時原模型需要刪除及重新求解的項目。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase water pressure on each plane separately and compare resistance sensitivity. Draw the case where one plane loses contact and identify terms that must be removed or solved again in the revised model.","failure":"注意干擾：一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用立體節理圖先確認共同交線與出露條件，再將每面水壓與反力方向畫出。比較乾季和雨季的孔壓變化，若只有一面明顯反應，應保留兩面差異，不用平均水壓抹平主導失效路徑。","textEn":"Use a three-dimensional joint diagram to establish intersection and daylighting, then show pressure and reaction on each plane. Compare seasonal pressures; if one plane responds strongly, retain that distinction rather than averaging pressure and concealing the controlling resistance path.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別提高第一面與第二面水壓，計算抗力變化並比較敏感度，再畫出一面失去接觸時原模型需要刪除及重新求解的項目。","textEn":"Increase water pressure on each plane separately and compare resistance sensitivity. Draw the case where one plane loses contact and identify terms that must be removed or solved again in the revised model.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙滑面岩楔抗力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Two plane wedge resistance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據","用立體節理圖先確認共同交線與出露條件，再將每面水壓與反力方向畫出。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly.","Use a three-dimensional joint diagram to establish intersection and daylighting, then show pressure and reaction on each plane."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用立體節理圖先確認共同交線與出露條件，再將每面水壓與反力方向畫出。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use a three-dimensional joint diagram to establish intersection and daylighting, then show pressure and reaction on each plane. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b207-v15-12","title":"雙滑面岩楔抗力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Two plane wedge resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙滑面岩楔抗力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Two plane wedge resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values. If a plane separates, its previous friction contribution cannot remain in the account; kinematics and equilibrium must be recalculated for the changed contact state. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：兩面抗力在真實空間須按向量合成，本例同方向相加是額外假設，不能直接轉用到不同交線方位。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Resistance contributions require vector combination in real space; adding them along one direction is an extra assumption here and cannot transfer unchanged to other intersection geometries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。","textEn":"High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values. If a plane separates, its previous friction contribution cannot remain in the account; kinematics and equilibrium must be recalculated for the changed contact state.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙滑面岩楔抗力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Two plane wedge resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加"],"optionsEn":["High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b207-v15-13","title":"錨索長期力保留：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Long term anchor force retention: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「錨索長期力保留」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long term anchor force retention” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"預應力錨索鎖定後可能因鋼材鬆弛、岩體變形及接頭就位而損失拉力，各效應的參考狀態必須說清楚。若後一比例作用於已減少的力，應連乘而非把百分率任意相加。教材只建立保留力帳，實際錨固區承載及防蝕完整性仍要獨立評估。 保留力與可承受最大力不同，前者描述目前預應力，後者還需要鋼材截面、錨頭與岩體黏結能力等證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「錨索長期力保留」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After lock-off, anchor force can decrease through steel relaxation, rock movement and seating, with each loss needing a stated reference state. If a later percentage acts on the remaining force, multiply retention factors rather than casually adding percentages. This account does not establish anchorage capacity or the integrity of corrosion protection. Retained force describes current prestress rather than maximum capacity; capacity additionally needs evidence about steel section, anchor head and rock-bond resistance along the system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long term anchor force retention” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「錨索長期力保留」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Long term anchor force retention”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-13-k1","title":"錨索長期力保留","titleEn":"Long term anchor force retention","text":"預應力錨索鎖定後可能因鋼材鬆弛、岩體變形及接頭就位而損失拉力，各效應的參考狀態必須說清楚。若後一比例作用於已減少的力，應連乘而非把百分率任意相加。","textEn":"After lock-off, anchor force can decrease through steel relaxation, rock movement and seating, with each loss needing a stated reference state. If a later percentage acts on the remaining force, multiply retention factors rather than casually adding percentages.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「錨索長期力保留」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long term anchor force retention\" is correct?","options":["所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加","預應力錨索鎖定後可能因鋼材鬆弛、岩體變形及接頭就位而損失拉力，各效應的參考狀態必須說清楚。","理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心"],"optionsEn":["All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states.","After lock-off, anchor force can decrease through steel relaxation, rock movement and seating, with each loss needing a stated reference state.","The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole."],"answer":1,"explanation":"預應力錨索鎖定後可能因鋼材鬆弛、岩體變形及接頭就位而損失拉力，各效應的參考狀態必須說清楚。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After lock-off, anchor force can decrease through steel relaxation, rock movement and seating, with each loss needing a stated reference state. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b207-v15-14","title":"錨索長期力保留：定量估算","titleEn":"Long term anchor force retention: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「錨索長期力保留」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long term anchor force retention” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN。模型邊界：兩個假想依序比例損失，並非現地錨索長期衰減定律。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN. Model boundary: two assumed sequential proportional losses, not a field law for anchor deterioration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將張拉、鎖定與後續量測的時間及溫度分別記錄，對照載重計校準與重新提離試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record stressing, lock-off and later readings with times and temperatures, checking load-cell calibration against lift-off testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN。模型邊界：兩個假想依序比例損失，並非現地錨索長期衰減定律。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN. Model boundary: two assumed sequential proportional losses, not a field law for anchor deterioration.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「錨索長期力保留」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long term anchor force retention\", which statement holds?","options":["單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度","相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening.","Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.","Original hypothetical example."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b207-v15-15","title":"錨索長期力保留：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long term anchor force retention: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「錨索長期力保留」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long term anchor force retention” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將張拉、鎖定與後續量測的時間及溫度分別記錄，對照載重計校準與重新提離試驗。若多支同時下降，先查共同岩體位移或溫度；若單支突變，則需檢查接頭滑移及儀器。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record stressing, lock-off and later readings with times and temperatures, checking load-cell calibration against lift-off testing. A coherent decline across anchors suggests shared rock movement or temperature, while one abrupt change requires investigation of connection slip or measurement failure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較依序損失與兩項皆以初始力為基準的算法，算出差值，再列出鎖定力、提離力與載重計讀值各自的測試邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare sequential losses with two losses both referenced to initial force and calculate the difference. Define the distinct measurement boundaries of lock-off force, lift-off force and load-cell readings.","failure":"注意干擾：接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將張拉、鎖定與後續量測的時間及溫度分別記錄，對照載重計校準與重新提離試驗。若多支同時下降，先查共同岩體位移或溫度；若單支突變，則需檢查接頭滑移及儀器。","textEn":"Record stressing, lock-off and later readings with times and temperatures, checking load-cell calibration against lift-off testing. A coherent decline across anchors suggests shared rock movement or temperature, while one abrupt change requires investigation of connection slip or measurement failure.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較依序損失與兩項皆以初始力為基準的算法，算出差值，再列出鎖定力、提離力與載重計讀值各自的測試邊界。","textEn":"Compare sequential losses with two losses both referenced to initial force and calculate the difference. Define the distinct measurement boundaries of lock-off force, lift-off force and load-cell readings.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「錨索長期力保留」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long term anchor force retention\"?","options":["將張拉、鎖定與後續量測的時間及溫度分別記錄，對照載重計校準與重新提離試驗。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深"],"optionsEn":["Record stressing, lock-off and later readings with times and temperatures, checking load-cell calibration against lift-off testing.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將張拉、鎖定與後續量測的時間及溫度分別記錄，對照載重計校準與重新提離試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record stressing, lock-off and later readings with times and temperatures, checking load-cell calibration against lift-off testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b207-v15-16","title":"錨索長期力保留：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long term anchor force retention: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「錨索長期力保留」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long term anchor force retention” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay. Corroded wire breaks can reduce redundancy without a large change in mean measured force, so one force history cannot demonstrate integrity of the complete anchoring system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：保留力與可承受最大力不同，前者描述目前預應力，後者還需要鋼材截面、錨頭與岩體黏結能力等證據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retained force describes current prestress rather than maximum capacity; capacity additionally needs evidence about steel section, anchor head and rock-bond resistance along the system.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。","textEn":"Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay. Corroded wire breaks can reduce redundancy without a large change in mean measured force, so one force history cannot demonstrate integrity of the complete anchoring system.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「錨索長期力保留」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long term anchor force retention\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。","理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay.","The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b207-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「挑流水舌射程」與「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ski jump jet travel\" and \"Jet impact pressure scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b207-v15-17","title":"挑流水舌射程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ski jump jet travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「挑流水舌射程」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ski jump jet travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"挑流水舌離開鼻坎後同時具有水平及垂直速度，重力使其軌跡彎曲。教材使用水平射出的拋體模型估算射程，只用來檢查尺度及方向；真實水舌會含氣、破碎並受尾水與風影響，不能以理想落點直接決定沖刷坑位置或岩體穩定。 水平射出時下落時間由高差決定，但若鼻坎提供向上速度，需解完整垂向方程，不能沿用相同飛行時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「挑流水舌射程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A ski-jump jet has horizontal and vertical velocity components and follows a gravity-curved trajectory. A horizontally launched projectile estimates travel scale and direction only. Real jets aerate, break up and interact with wind and tailwater, so an ideal impact point does not directly locate scour or establish rock stability. For horizontal launch, drop determines flight time; an upward launch component requires the full vertical equation and cannot retain the same time of flight. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ski jump jet travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「挑流水舌射程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ski jump jet travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-17-k1","title":"挑流水舌射程","titleEn":"Ski jump jet travel","text":"挑流水舌離開鼻坎後同時具有水平及垂直速度，重力使其軌跡彎曲。教材使用水平射出的拋體模型估算射程，只用來檢查尺度及方向；真實水舌會含氣、破碎並受尾水與風影響，不能以理想落點直接決定沖刷坑位置或岩體穩定。","textEn":"A ski-jump jet has horizontal and vertical velocity components and follows a gravity-curved trajectory. A horizontally launched projectile estimates travel scale and direction only.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「挑流水舌射程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ski jump jet travel\" is correct?","options":["理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心","所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加","挑流水舌離開鼻坎後同時具有水平及垂直速度，重力使其軌跡彎曲。"],"optionsEn":["The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole.","Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.","A ski-jump jet has horizontal and vertical velocity components and follows a gravity-curved trajectory."],"answer":2,"explanation":"挑流水舌離開鼻坎後同時具有水平及垂直速度，重力使其軌跡彎曲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A ski-jump jet has horizontal and vertical velocity components and follows a gravity-curved trajectory. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b207-v15-18","title":"挑流水舌射程：定量估算","titleEn":"Ski jump jet travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「挑流水舌射程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ski jump jet travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m。模型邊界：水平初速且初始垂直速度為零的真空拋體，忽略水舌破碎。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m. Model boundary: horizontal launch with zero initial vertical velocity in a drag-free projectile model, excluding jet breakup. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以影像追蹤水舌外緣與中心線，核對出射角及速度範圍，再比較不同流量的落水帶寬度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track the jet envelope and centerline with imagery, checking launch angle and velocity range, then compare impact-zone width at different discharges.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m。模型邊界：水平初速且初始垂直速度為零的真空拋體，忽略水舌破碎。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m. Model boundary: horizontal launch with zero initial vertical velocity in a drag-free projectile model, excluding jet breakup.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「挑流水舌射程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ski jump jet travel\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m。","出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失","兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m.","A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir.","Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b207-v15-19","title":"挑流水舌射程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ski jump jet travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「挑流水舌射程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ski jump jet travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以影像追蹤水舌外緣與中心線，核對出射角及速度範圍，再比較不同流量的落水帶寬度。若落點展寬而中心位置近似不變，應研究破碎與含氣，不能只調整平均出射速度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track the jet envelope and centerline with imagery, checking launch angle and velocity range, then compare impact-zone width at different discharges. A wider landing band with a similar center suggests breakup or aeration rather than merely a change in average launch speed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以兩個水平速度計算射程，再加入向上出射的概念軌跡，說明需要哪些影像及尾水資料才能從教材拋體轉向實際水舌分析。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate range at two horizontal speeds, then sketch an upward-launched case. Identify image and tailwater data needed to progress from the teaching projectile to analysis of a real spillway jet.","failure":"注意干擾：出射角或流束不均會使局部水舌偏向邊坡，即使平均射程符合估算仍有側向衝擊；忽略尾水淹沒也會錯估真正能量耗散區域。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven flow or launch angle can direct part of the jet toward a slope even when mean range matches the calculation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以影像追蹤水舌外緣與中心線，核對出射角及速度範圍，再比較不同流量的落水帶寬度。若落點展寬而中心位置近似不變，應研究破碎與含氣，不能只調整平均出射速度。","textEn":"Track the jet envelope and centerline with imagery, checking launch angle and velocity range, then compare impact-zone width at different discharges. A wider landing band with a similar center suggests breakup or aeration rather than merely a change in average launch speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以兩個水平速度計算射程，再加入向上出射的概念軌跡，說明需要哪些影像及尾水資料才能從教材拋體轉向實際水舌分析。","textEn":"Calculate range at two horizontal speeds, then sketch an upward-launched case. Identify image and tailwater data needed to progress from the teaching projectile to analysis of a real spillway jet.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「挑流水舌射程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ski jump jet travel\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以影像追蹤水舌外緣與中心線，核對出射角及速度範圍，再比較不同流量的落水帶寬度。","平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Track the jet envelope and centerline with imagery, checking launch angle and velocity range, then compare impact-zone width at different discharges.","Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以影像追蹤水舌外緣與中心線，核對出射角及速度範圍，再比較不同流量的落水帶寬度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track the jet envelope and centerline with imagery, checking launch angle and velocity range, then compare impact-zone width at different discharges. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b207-v15-20","title":"挑流水舌射程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ski jump jet travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「挑流水舌射程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ski jump jet travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出射角或流束不均會使局部水舌偏向邊坡，即使平均射程符合估算仍有側向衝擊；忽略尾水淹沒也會錯估真正能量耗散區域。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven flow or launch angle can direct part of the jet toward a slope even when mean range matches the calculation. Ignoring tailwater submergence additionally misidentifies where the jet actually dissipates its energy and transfers momentum. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：水平射出時下落時間由高差決定，但若鼻坎提供向上速度，需解完整垂向方程，不能沿用相同飛行時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: For horizontal launch, drop determines flight time; an upward launch component requires the full vertical equation and cannot retain the same time of flight.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出射角或流束不均會使局部水舌偏向邊坡，即使平均射程符合估算仍有側向衝擊；忽略尾水淹沒也會錯估真正能量耗散區域。","textEn":"Uneven flow or launch angle can direct part of the jet toward a slope even when mean range matches the calculation. Ignoring tailwater submergence additionally misidentifies where the jet actually dissipates its energy and transfers momentum.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「挑流水舌射程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ski jump jet travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加","出射角或流束不均會使局部水舌偏向邊坡，即使平均射程符合估算仍有側向衝擊；忽略尾水淹沒也會錯估真正能量耗散區域。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.","Uneven flow or launch angle can direct part of the jet toward a slope even when mean range matches the calculation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"出射角或流束不均會使局部水舌偏向邊坡，即使平均射程符合估算仍有側向衝擊；忽略尾水淹沒也會錯估真正能量耗散區域。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven flow or launch angle can direct part of the jet toward a slope even when mean range matches the calculation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b207-v15-21","title":"水舌衝擊壓力尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Jet impact pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Jet impact pressure scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水舌速度在撞擊區轉成壓力與湍流，動壓提供一個能量密度尺度，但瞬時壓力分布取決於水舌破碎、尾水深度和岩面形狀。動壓不是整片底床均勻承受的壓力，亦不能直接乘任意面積得到設計合力。需同時掌握受力面積與時間統計。 動壓的帕斯卡與每立方米焦耳量綱相同，代表能量密度而非總能量，乘體積或面積後才得到不同物理量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Jet velocity is converted into pressure and turbulence at impact. Dynamic pressure supplies an energy-density scale, while instantaneous distribution depends on breakup, tailwater depth and bed geometry. It is not uniform over the whole bed and cannot be multiplied by an arbitrary area to obtain a design resultant without spatial and temporal evidence. Pascals share dimensions with joules per cubic metre, expressing energy density rather than total energy; multiplying by volume or area produces different physical quantities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet impact pressure scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet impact pressure scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-21-k1","title":"水舌衝擊壓力尺度","titleEn":"Jet impact pressure scale","text":"水舌速度在撞擊區轉成壓力與湍流，動壓提供一個能量密度尺度，但瞬時壓力分布取決於水舌破碎、尾水深度和岩面形狀。動壓不是整片底床均勻承受的壓力，亦不能直接乘任意面積得到設計合力。","textEn":"Jet velocity is converted into pressure and turbulence at impact. Dynamic pressure supplies an energy-density scale, while instantaneous distribution depends on breakup, tailwater depth and bed geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Jet impact pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["水舌速度在撞擊區轉成壓力與湍流，動壓提供一個能量密度尺度，但瞬時壓力分布取決於水舌破碎、尾水深度和岩面形狀。","所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加","單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度"],"optionsEn":["Jet velocity is converted into pressure and turbulence at impact.","Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.","Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水舌速度在撞擊區轉成壓力與湍流，動壓提供一個能量密度尺度，但瞬時壓力分布取決於水舌破碎、尾水深度和岩面形狀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Jet velocity is converted into pressure and turbulence at impact. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b207-v15-22","title":"水舌衝擊壓力尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Jet impact pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Jet impact pressure scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa。模型邊界：單相速度的動壓尺度，不是沖刷坑底實測峰值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa. Model boundary: dynamic-pressure scale for single-phase velocity, not a measured plunge-pool bottom peak. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在模型或合適量測資料中比較不同位置的平均、峰值與相關性，核對感測器頻寬及通氣影響。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare mean pressure, peaks and spatial correlation using model or suitable measured data, checking sensor bandwidth and aeration effects.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa。模型邊界：單相速度的動壓尺度，不是沖刷坑底實測峰值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa. Model boundary: dynamic-pressure scale for single-phase velocity, not a measured plunge-pool bottom peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Jet impact pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa。","壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深"],"optionsEn":["Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa.","Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b207-v15-23","title":"水舌衝擊壓力尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Jet impact pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Jet impact pressure scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在模型或合適量測資料中比較不同位置的平均、峰值與相關性，核對感測器頻寬及通氣影響。若鄰近測點峰值不同時發生，不能把各點最大值同時相加成總力，需保留同步壓力場。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare mean pressure, peaks and spatial correlation using model or suitable measured data, checking sensor bandwidth and aeration effects. Peaks at neighboring locations that occur at different times cannot simply be added into one total force; retain synchronized pressure fields for integration. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將速度提高一成計算動壓變化，再建立兩個不同相位的壓力時序，對比逐點最大值總和與同步積分最大值的差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase velocity by ten percent and recalculate dynamic pressure. Create two out-of-phase pressure histories and compare the sum of individual maxima with the maximum of their synchronized integral.","failure":"注意干擾：岩節理中的壓力脈動可能向內傳播並抬動岩塊，即使表面平均壓力不高；含氣改變可壓縮性與脈動傳遞，因此清水動壓尺度無法單獨描述剝離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pressure fluctuations can penetrate rock joints and lift blocks despite modest mean surface pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在模型或合適量測資料中比較不同位置的平均、峰值與相關性，核對感測器頻寬及通氣影響。若鄰近測點峰值不同時發生，不能把各點最大值同時相加成總力，需保留同步壓力場。","textEn":"Compare mean pressure, peaks and spatial correlation using model or suitable measured data, checking sensor bandwidth and aeration effects. Peaks at neighboring locations that occur at different times cannot simply be added into one total force; retain synchronized pressure fields for integration.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將速度提高一成計算動壓變化，再建立兩個不同相位的壓力時序，對比逐點最大值總和與同步積分最大值的差異。","textEn":"Increase velocity by ten percent and recalculate dynamic pressure. Create two out-of-phase pressure histories and compare the sum of individual maxima with the maximum of their synchronized integral.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Jet impact pressure scale\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分","在模型或合適量測資料中比較不同位置的平均、峰值與相關性，核對感測器頻寬及通氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.","Compare mean pressure, peaks and spatial correlation using model or suitable measured data, checking sensor bandwidth and aeration effects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在模型或合適量測資料中比較不同位置的平均、峰值與相關性，核對感測器頻寬及通氣影響。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare mean pressure, peaks and spatial correlation using model or suitable measured data, checking sensor bandwidth and aeration effects. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b207-v15-24","title":"水舌衝擊壓力尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Jet impact pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Jet impact pressure scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"岩節理中的壓力脈動可能向內傳播並抬動岩塊，即使表面平均壓力不高；含氣改變可壓縮性與脈動傳遞，因此清水動壓尺度無法單獨描述剝離。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pressure fluctuations can penetrate rock joints and lift blocks despite modest mean surface pressure. Aeration changes compressibility and fluctuation transmission, so a clear-water dynamic-pressure scale alone cannot describe block removal or the progression of scour. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：動壓的帕斯卡與每立方米焦耳量綱相同，代表能量密度而非總能量，乘體積或面積後才得到不同物理量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pascals share dimensions with joules per cubic metre, expressing energy density rather than total energy; multiplying by volume or area produces different physical quantities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"岩節理中的壓力脈動可能向內傳播並抬動岩塊，即使表面平均壓力不高；含氣改變可壓縮性與脈動傳遞，因此清水動壓尺度無法單獨描述剝離。","textEn":"Pressure fluctuations can penetrate rock joints and lift blocks despite modest mean surface pressure. Aeration changes compressibility and fluctuation transmission, so a clear-water dynamic-pressure scale alone cannot describe block removal or the progression of scour.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Jet impact pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["岩節理中的壓力脈動可能向內傳播並抬動岩塊，即使表面平均壓力不高；含氣改變可壓縮性與脈動傳遞，因此清水動壓尺度無法單獨描述剝離。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度"],"optionsEn":["Pressure fluctuations can penetrate rock joints and lift blocks despite modest mean surface pressure.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岩節理中的壓力脈動可能向內傳播並抬動岩塊，即使表面平均壓力不高；含氣改變可壓縮性與脈動傳遞，因此清水動壓尺度無法單獨描述剝離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pressure fluctuations can penetrate rock joints and lift blocks despite modest mean surface pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b207-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「壩塊自由收縮」與「分層交換位能」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Dam block free contraction\" and \"Stratified exchange potential energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b207-v15-25","title":"壩塊自由收縮：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dam block free contraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「壩塊自由收縮」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dam block free contraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高壩混凝土塊體降溫會產生自由收縮，但拱圈閉合、岩體約束及灌漿時機會決定實際縫寬與應力。教材先算一段假想塊體的自由長度減少，明確以幅度表示；不能把它直接當接縫開度，因相鄰塊體也在變形且整體幾何可能限制位移。 相鄰塊體各自的無應力溫度未必相同，接縫灌漿年代及材料齡期會改變後續收縮的參考狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壩塊自由收縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cooling a high-dam concrete block creates free contraction, while arch closure, rock restraint and grouting timing determine actual joint opening and stress. Compute the magnitude of free shortening in an assumed block first. It is not directly the joint opening because neighboring blocks deform and the overall geometry can restrain movement. Neighboring blocks may have different stress-free temperatures; grouting history and material age change the reference state from which subsequent contraction and restraint develop. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dam block free contraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壩塊自由收縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dam block free contraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-25-k1","title":"壩塊自由收縮","titleEn":"Dam block free contraction","text":"高壩混凝土塊體降溫會產生自由收縮，但拱圈閉合、岩體約束及灌漿時機會決定實際縫寬與應力。教材先算一段假想塊體的自由長度減少，明確以幅度表示；不能把它直接當接縫開度，因相鄰塊體也在變形且整體幾何可能限制位移。","textEn":"Cooling a high-dam concrete block creates free contraction, while arch closure, rock restraint and grouting timing determine actual joint opening and stress. Compute the magnitude of free shortening in an assumed block first.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壩塊自由收縮」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dam block free contraction\" is correct?","options":["單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度","高壩混凝土塊體降溫會產生自由收縮，但拱圈閉合、岩體約束及灌漿時機會決定實際縫寬與應力。","出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失"],"optionsEn":["Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening.","Cooling a high-dam concrete block creates free contraction, while arch closure, rock restraint and grouting timing determine actual joint opening and stress.","A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高壩混凝土塊體降溫會產生自由收縮，但拱圈閉合、岩體約束及灌漿時機會決定實際縫寬與應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cooling a high-dam concrete block creates free contraction, while arch closure, rock restraint and grouting timing determine actual joint opening and stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b207-v15-26","title":"壩塊自由收縮：定量估算","titleEn":"Dam block free contraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壩塊自由收縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dam block free contraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm。模型邊界：均勻降溫的自由收縮幅度，不含相鄰塊體與約束。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm. Model boundary: free-shortening magnitude for uniform cooling, excluding neighboring blocks and restraint. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時比較塊內溫度剖面與接縫兩側位移，核對降溫是否均勻及量測正向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare internal temperature profiles with displacement on both sides of the joint, checking uniformity and sign conventions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm。模型邊界：均勻降溫的自由收縮幅度，不含相鄰塊體與約束。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm. Model boundary: free-shortening magnitude for uniform cooling, excluding neighboring blocks and restraint.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壩塊自由收縮」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dam block free contraction\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據","平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly.","Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=20 m; dTcool=15 K; shortening=alpha*L*dTcool*1000=3 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b207-v15-27","title":"壩塊自由收縮：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dam block free contraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壩塊自由收縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dam block free contraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時比較塊內溫度剖面與接縫兩側位移，核對降溫是否均勻及量測正向。若兩側都朝同方向移動，接縫差值可能很小但整體位移不小，應分別呈現絕對與相對運動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare internal temperature profiles with displacement on both sides of the joint, checking uniformity and sign conventions. If both sides move in the same direction, relative opening may be small despite substantial overall movement, so present absolute and relative components separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為兩個相鄰塊體設定不同降溫，計算各自自由收縮，再畫共同平移與相對開縫兩種位移場，指出需要哪些量測才能區分。","observationEn":"Site practice: Assign different cooling changes to two neighboring blocks and calculate free shortening. Draw common translation and relative opening fields, identifying the measurements needed to distinguish them rather than relying on one gauge.","failure":"注意干擾：用單側位移當縫寬會把整體平移誤算為開裂，溫度梯度又可能造成彎曲而非純收縮；若只保存平均溫度，將失去辨認兩種機制的關鍵資訊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using one-side displacement as joint width mistakes translation for opening, while a temperature gradient can produce bending rather than pure shortening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時比較塊內溫度剖面與接縫兩側位移，核對降溫是否均勻及量測正向。若兩側都朝同方向移動，接縫差值可能很小但整體位移不小，應分別呈現絕對與相對運動。","textEn":"Compare internal temperature profiles with displacement on both sides of the joint, checking uniformity and sign conventions. If both sides move in the same direction, relative opening may be small despite substantial overall movement, so present absolute and relative components separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為兩個相鄰塊體設定不同降溫，計算各自自由收縮，再畫共同平移與相對開縫兩種位移場，指出需要哪些量測才能區分。","textEn":"Assign different cooling changes to two neighboring blocks and calculate free shortening. Draw common translation and relative opening fields, identifying the measurements needed to distinguish them rather than relying on one gauge.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壩塊自由收縮」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dam block free contraction\"?","options":["同時比較塊內溫度剖面與接縫兩側位移，核對降溫是否均勻及量測正向。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加"],"optionsEn":["Compare internal temperature profiles with displacement on both sides of the joint, checking uniformity and sign conventions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時比較塊內溫度剖面與接縫兩側位移，核對降溫是否均勻及量測正向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare internal temperature profiles with displacement on both sides of the joint, checking uniformity and sign conventions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b207-v15-28","title":"壩塊自由收縮：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dam block free contraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壩塊自由收縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dam block free contraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用單側位移當縫寬會把整體平移誤算為開裂，溫度梯度又可能造成彎曲而非純收縮；若只保存平均溫度，將失去辨認兩種機制的關鍵資訊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using one-side displacement as joint width mistakes translation for opening, while a temperature gradient can produce bending rather than pure shortening. Retaining only average temperature removes information needed to distinguish those mechanisms in the observed movement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相鄰塊體各自的無應力溫度未必相同，接縫灌漿年代及材料齡期會改變後續收縮的參考狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Neighboring blocks may have different stress-free temperatures; grouting history and material age change the reference state from which subsequent contraction and restraint develop.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用單側位移當縫寬會把整體平移誤算為開裂，溫度梯度又可能造成彎曲而非純收縮；若只保存平均溫度，將失去辨認兩種機制的關鍵資訊。","textEn":"Using one-side displacement as joint width mistakes translation for opening, while a temperature gradient can produce bending rather than pure shortening. Retaining only average temperature removes information needed to distinguish those mechanisms in the observed movement.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壩塊自由收縮」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dam block free contraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用單側位移當縫寬會把整體平移誤算為開裂，溫度梯度又可能造成彎曲而非純收縮；若只保存平均溫度，將失去辨認兩種機制的關鍵資訊。","出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using one-side displacement as joint width mistakes translation for opening, while a temperature gradient can produce bending rather than pure shortening.","A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用單側位移當縫寬會把整體平移誤算為開裂，溫度梯度又可能造成彎曲而非純收縮；若只保存平均溫度，將失去辨認兩種機制的關鍵資訊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using one-side displacement as joint width mistakes translation for opening, while a temperature gradient can produce bending rather than pure shortening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b207-v15-29","title":"分層交換位能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stratified exchange potential energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「分層交換位能」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stratified exchange potential energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。教材以兩等體積水團交換高程的位能差說明密度影響，不把此值當成實際混合所需總功。湍流耗散、界面厚度及連續剖面會改變能量路徑，取水溫度控制仍需觀察真正吸入水層。 兩水團交換時各自有位能變化，將兩者相加才留下密度差項，不能把完整水密度直接代入浮力差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分層交換位能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Exchanging upper and lower reservoir layers works against buoyancy associated with density contrast. The potential-energy change for equal exchanged volumes illustrates that effect but is not the total work required for actual mixing. Turbulent dissipation, interface thickness and continuous density profiles alter the energy pathway and withdrawal behavior. Both exchanged parcels change potential energy; adding their contributions leaves the density-contrast term, rather than permitting full water density to represent the buoyancy difference. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stratified exchange potential energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ.","failure":"常見誤解：「出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分層交換位能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stratified exchange potential energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-29-k1","title":"分層交換位能","titleEn":"Stratified exchange potential energy","text":"分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。教材以兩等體積水團交換高程的位能差說明密度影響，不把此值當成實際混合所需總功。","textEn":"Exchanging upper and lower reservoir layers works against buoyancy associated with density contrast. The potential-energy change for equal exchanged volumes illustrates that effect but is not the total work required for actual mixing.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分層交換位能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stratified exchange potential energy\" is correct?","options":["出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失","相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能","分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。"],"optionsEn":["A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir.","Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.","Exchanging upper and lower reservoir layers works against buoyancy associated with density contrast."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Exchanging upper and lower reservoir layers works against buoyancy associated with density contrast. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b207-v15-30","title":"分層交換位能：定量估算","titleEn":"Stratified exchange potential energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分層交換位能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stratified exchange potential energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ。模型邊界：上輕下重兩等體積水團交換位置的位能增加，忽略混合耗散。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ. Model boundary: potential-energy increase from swapping equal light-upper and dense-lower volumes, excluding mixing dissipation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以密度剖面確認上下層排列，核對水團體積及高程差定義，再將取水前後剖面比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the upper-light lower-dense arrangement using density profiles, define exchanged volume and elevation difference, and compare profiles before and after withdrawal.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ。模型邊界：上輕下重兩等體積水團交換位置的位能增加，忽略混合耗散。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ. Model boundary: potential-energy increase from swapping equal light-upper and dense-lower volumes, excluding mixing dissipation.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分層交換位能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stratified exchange potential energy\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ。","壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深","兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example.","Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration.","Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b207-v15-31","title":"分層交換位能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stratified exchange potential energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分層交換位能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stratified exchange potential energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以密度剖面確認上下層排列，核對水團體積及高程差定義，再將取水前後剖面比較。若溫度改變但密度界面仍存在，不能宣稱整庫已混合；需分辨局部置換、捲吸與全深混合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the upper-light lower-dense arrangement using density profiles, define exchanged volume and elevation difference, and compare profiles before and after withdrawal. Changed outlet temperature with an intact interface does not demonstrate complete reservoir mixing; distinguish local replacement, entrainment and full-depth mixing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將密度差減半重算交換位能，保持總熱量相同卻改變垂向分布，說明何種剖面量測可辨認不同浮力結構及取水反應。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve density contrast and recalculate exchange energy. Keep total heat unchanged while altering its vertical distribution, and identify profile measurements that distinguish buoyancy structures and withdrawal responses.","failure":"注意干擾：僅用出口溫度判斷分層消失，可能漏掉深層冷水仍被隔離的情況；含砂入流也可改變密度而非單純改變溫度，使熱量與浮力的推論分歧。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Outlet temperature alone can conceal an isolated cold deep layer and falsely suggest lost stratification. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以密度剖面確認上下層排列，核對水團體積及高程差定義，再將取水前後剖面比較。若溫度改變但密度界面仍存在，不能宣稱整庫已混合；需分辨局部置換、捲吸與全深混合。","textEn":"Verify the upper-light lower-dense arrangement using density profiles, define exchanged volume and elevation difference, and compare profiles before and after withdrawal. Changed outlet temperature with an intact interface does not demonstrate complete reservoir mixing; distinguish local replacement, entrainment and full-depth mixing.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將密度差減半重算交換位能，保持總熱量相同卻改變垂向分布，說明何種剖面量測可辨認不同浮力結構及取水反應。","textEn":"Halve density contrast and recalculate exchange energy. Keep total heat unchanged while altering its vertical distribution, and identify profile measurements that distinguish buoyancy structures and withdrawal responses.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分層交換位能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stratified exchange potential energy\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以密度剖面確認上下層排列，核對水團體積及高程差定義，再將取水前後剖面比較。","理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Verify the upper-light lower-dense arrangement using density profiles, define exchanged volume and elevation difference, and compare profiles before and after withdrawal.","The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以密度剖面確認上下層排列，核對水團體積及高程差定義，再將取水前後剖面比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the upper-light lower-dense arrangement using density profiles, define exchanged volume and elevation difference, and compare profiles before and after withdrawal. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b207-v15-32","title":"分層交換位能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stratified exchange potential energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分層交換位能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stratified exchange potential energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"僅用出口溫度判斷分層消失，可能漏掉深層冷水仍被隔離的情況；含砂入流也可改變密度而非單純改變溫度，使熱量與浮力的推論分歧。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Outlet temperature alone can conceal an isolated cold deep layer and falsely suggest lost stratification. Sediment-laden inflow can also change density without an equivalent temperature change, separating thermal interpretation from the actual buoyancy structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：兩水團交換時各自有位能變化，將兩者相加才留下密度差項，不能把完整水密度直接代入浮力差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Both exchanged parcels change potential energy; adding their contributions leaves the density-contrast term, rather than permitting full water density to represent the buoyancy difference.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"僅用出口溫度判斷分層消失，可能漏掉深層冷水仍被隔離的情況；含砂入流也可改變密度而非單純改變溫度，使熱量與浮力的推論分歧。","textEn":"Outlet temperature alone can conceal an isolated cold deep layer and falsely suggest lost stratification. Sediment-laden inflow can also change density without an equivalent temperature change, separating thermal interpretation from the actual buoyancy structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分層交換位能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stratified exchange potential energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能","僅用出口溫度判斷分層消失，可能漏掉深層冷水仍被隔離的情況；含砂入流也可改變密度而非單純改變溫度，使熱量與浮力的推論分歧。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.","Outlet temperature alone can conceal an isolated cold deep layer and falsely suggest lost stratification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"僅用出口溫度判斷分層消失，可能漏掉深層冷水仍被隔離的情況；含砂入流也可改變密度而非單純改變溫度，使熱量與浮力的推論分歧。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Outlet temperature alone can conceal an isolated cold deep layer and falsely suggest lost stratification. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b207-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「調蓄水的能量尺度」與「相關監測聯合殘差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stored water energy scale\" and \"Correlated monitoring residuals\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b207-v15-33","title":"調蓄水的能量尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stored water energy scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「調蓄水的能量尺度」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stored water energy scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"儲水的可發電能量取決於放水時的淨水頭及效率，並非單由庫容決定。以固定水頭近似可先估算一小段水量的能量尺度，但大量放水會改變上下游水位，需沿儲量積分。水體還可能有灌溉與環境用途，所以潛在電能不等於可全部出售的電量。 能量換算需從焦耳轉為瓦時再轉為吉瓦時，忽略每小時秒數會造成巨大單位錯誤，應逐級檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「調蓄水的能量尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stored-water generation depends on net head and efficiency during release, not storage volume alone. Constant head estimates the energy scale of a limited volume, while major drawdown requires integrating changing head with storage. Other water uses further distinguish potential electrical energy from energy actually available for sale. Energy conversion must connect joules to watt-hours and then gigawatt-hours; omitting seconds per hour causes a major unit error that dimensional steps should expose. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stored water energy scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「調蓄水的能量尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stored water energy scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-33-k1","title":"調蓄水的能量尺度","titleEn":"Stored water energy scale","text":"儲水的可發電能量取決於放水時的淨水頭及效率，並非單由庫容決定。以固定水頭近似可先估算一小段水量的能量尺度，但大量放水會改變上下游水位，需沿儲量積分。","textEn":"Stored-water generation depends on net head and efficiency during release, not storage volume alone. Constant head estimates the energy scale of a limited volume, while major drawdown requires integrating changing head with storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「調蓄水的能量尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stored water energy scale\" is correct?","options":["儲水的可發電能量取決於放水時的淨水頭及效率，並非單由庫容決定。","相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能","兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據"],"optionsEn":["Stored-water generation depends on net head and efficiency during release, not storage volume alone.","Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.","Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"儲水的可發電能量取決於放水時的淨水頭及效率，並非單由庫容決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stored-water generation depends on net head and efficiency during release, not storage volume alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b207-v15-34","title":"調蓄水的能量尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Stored water energy scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「調蓄水的能量尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stored water energy scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh。模型邊界：固定淨水頭效率且假設全量經機組，不含其他用途與時序限制。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh. Model boundary: fixed net head and efficiency with all water passing through turbines, excluding other uses and timing constraints. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以分段放水量與各段平均淨水頭積分，對照固定水頭結果，再核對旁通及其他取水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate incremental releases using each segment mean net head and compare the fixed-head estimate, accounting for bypass and other withdrawals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh。模型邊界：固定淨水頭效率且假設全量經機組，不含其他用途與時序限制。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh. Model boundary: fixed net head and efficiency with all water passing through turbines, excluding other uses and timing constraints.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「調蓄水的能量尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stored water energy scale\", which statement holds?","options":["平均膜壓縮很大就不可能出現局部拉應力","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh。","所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加"],"optionsEn":["Large mean membrane compression makes local tensile stress impossible.","Original hypothetical example.","All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=20000000 m3; H=180 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); E=rho*g*V*H*eta/3.6e12=8.829 GWh. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b207-v15-35","title":"調蓄水的能量尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stored water energy scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「調蓄水的能量尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stored water energy scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以分段放水量與各段平均淨水頭積分，對照固定水頭結果，再核對旁通及其他取水。若庫水位下降明顯，應縮小分段以檢查收斂，不把最初最高水頭用於全部水量來高估能量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate incremental releases using each segment mean net head and compare the fixed-head estimate, accounting for bypass and other withdrawals. When level changes substantially, refine the segments and check convergence rather than applying the initial maximum head to every unit of water. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把水量分成兩段並給不同淨水頭，重算總電能，與固定平均及初始水頭兩種近似比較，再列出水庫用途約束對可用量的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Split release into two volumes with different net heads and calculate total energy. Compare fixed-average and initial-head approximations, then explain how water-use constraints alter the volume available for generation.","failure":"注意干擾：尾水隨出流上升會進一步降低淨水頭，僅考慮庫水位下降仍可能高估能量；若用總庫容替代可調節庫容，也會把不能利用的水列入電量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tailwater rising with release further reduces head, so accounting only for falling reservoir level may still overstate energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以分段放水量與各段平均淨水頭積分，對照固定水頭結果，再核對旁通及其他取水。若庫水位下降明顯，應縮小分段以檢查收斂，不把最初最高水頭用於全部水量來高估能量。","textEn":"Integrate incremental releases using each segment mean net head and compare the fixed-head estimate, accounting for bypass and other withdrawals. When level changes substantially, refine the segments and check convergence rather than applying the initial maximum head to every unit of water.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把水量分成兩段並給不同淨水頭，重算總電能，與固定平均及初始水頭兩種近似比較，再列出水庫用途約束對可用量的影響。","textEn":"Split release into two volumes with different net heads and calculate total energy. Compare fixed-average and initial-head approximations, then explain how water-use constraints alter the volume available for generation.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「調蓄水的能量尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stored water energy scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加","以分段放水量與各段平均淨水頭積分，對照固定水頭結果，再核對旁通及其他取水。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.","Integrate incremental releases using each segment mean net head and compare the fixed-head estimate, accounting for bypass and other withdrawals."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以分段放水量與各段平均淨水頭積分，對照固定水頭結果，再核對旁通及其他取水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate incremental releases using each segment mean net head and compare the fixed-head estimate, accounting for bypass and other withdrawals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b207-v15-36","title":"調蓄水的能量尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stored water energy scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「調蓄水的能量尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stored water energy scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"尾水隨出流上升會進一步降低淨水頭，僅考慮庫水位下降仍可能高估能量；若用總庫容替代可調節庫容，也會把不能利用的水列入電量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tailwater rising with release further reduces head, so accounting only for falling reservoir level may still overstate energy. Using total rather than usable storage can also include water that cannot be allocated to the assumed generating sequence. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：能量換算需從焦耳轉為瓦時再轉為吉瓦時，忽略每小時秒數會造成巨大單位錯誤，應逐級檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Energy conversion must connect joules to watt-hours and then gigawatt-hours; omitting seconds per hour causes a major unit error that dimensional steps should expose.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal storage volume represents equal electrical energy at every head.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"尾水隨出流上升會進一步降低淨水頭，僅考慮庫水位下降仍可能高估能量；若用總庫容替代可調節庫容，也會把不能利用的水列入電量。","textEn":"Tailwater rising with release further reduces head, so accounting only for falling reservoir level may still overstate energy. Using total rather than usable storage can also include water that cannot be allocated to the assumed generating sequence.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「調蓄水的能量尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stored water energy scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["尾水隨出流上升會進一步降低淨水頭，僅考慮庫水位下降仍可能高估能量；若用總庫容替代可調節庫容，也會把不能利用的水列入電量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據"],"optionsEn":["Tailwater rising with release further reduces head, so accounting only for falling reservoir level may still overstate energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"尾水隨出流上升會進一步降低淨水頭，僅考慮庫水位下降仍可能高估能量；若用總庫容替代可調節庫容，也會把不能利用的水列入電量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tailwater rising with release further reduces head, so accounting only for falling reservoir level may still overstate energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b207-v15-37","title":"相關監測聯合殘差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Correlated monitoring residuals: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「相關監測聯合殘差」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Correlated monitoring residuals” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壩體相鄰量測常因同一水位或溫度作用而相關，不能把每個偏離都當成獨立證據。教材以兩個標準化殘差與相關係數建立聯合距離，說明共同變動與相反變動具有不同意義。統計距離仍須依有效基線與物理機制解讀，不能直接當成安全分數。 相關係數接近一時矩陣可能病態，小量測差異會被大幅放大，應檢查基線品質與數值穩定性再解讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「相關監測聯合殘差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Nearby dam observations often correlate through shared level or temperature effects and cannot each be counted as independent evidence. A two-residual distance with correlation distinguishes common movement from opposing movement. Its interpretation still depends on a valid baseline and physical mechanism; the statistical distance is not a direct safety score. A correlation near one makes the covariance matrix ill-conditioned and can amplify small differences; assess baseline quality and numerical stability before interpreting the joint distance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Correlated monitoring residuals” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「相關監測聯合殘差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Correlated monitoring residuals”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-37-k1","title":"相關監測聯合殘差","titleEn":"Correlated monitoring residuals","text":"壩體相鄰量測常因同一水位或溫度作用而相關，不能把每個偏離都當成獨立證據。教材以兩個標準化殘差與相關係數建立聯合距離，說明共同變動與相反變動具有不同意義。","textEn":"Nearby dam observations often correlate through shared level or temperature effects and cannot each be counted as independent evidence. A two-residual distance with correlation distinguishes common movement from opposing movement.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「相關監測聯合殘差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Correlated monitoring residuals\" is correct?","options":["兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據","壩體相鄰量測常因同一水位或溫度作用而相關，不能把每個偏離都當成獨立證據。","壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深"],"optionsEn":["Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly.","Nearby dam observations often correlate through shared level or temperature effects and cannot each be counted as independent evidence.","Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壩體相鄰量測常因同一水位或溫度作用而相關，不能把每個偏離都當成獨立證據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Nearby dam observations often correlate through shared level or temperature effects and cannot each be counted as independent evidence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b207-v15-38","title":"相關監測聯合殘差：定量估算","titleEn":"Correlated monitoring residuals: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「相關監測聯合殘差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Correlated monitoring residuals” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444。模型邊界：兩個無因次標準化殘差及固定相關係數；只示範平方距離，未給警報門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444. Model boundary: two dimensionless standardized residuals with fixed correlation; squared-distance illustration without an alarm threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用未含已知異常的基線估計相關，檢查不同季節是否穩定，並與不同原理儀器比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate correlation from a baseline excluding known anomalies, test seasonal stability and compare instruments using different principles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444。模型邊界：兩個無因次標準化殘差及固定相關係數；只示範平方距離，未給警報門檻。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444. Model boundary: two dimensionless standardized residuals with fixed correlation; squared-distance illustration without an alarm threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「相關監測聯合殘差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Correlated monitoring residuals\", which statement holds?","options":["兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分","理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444。"],"optionsEn":["Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.","The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole.","Original hypothetical example."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: z1=2 (dimensionless); z2=2 (dimensionless); r=0.8 (dimensionless); D2=(z1*z1-2*r*z1*z2+z2*z2)/(1-r*r)=4.444444444. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b207-v15-39","title":"相關監測聯合殘差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Correlated monitoring residuals: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「相關監測聯合殘差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Correlated monitoring residuals” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用未含已知異常的基線估計相關，檢查不同季節是否穩定，並與不同原理儀器比對。若相關結構本身改變，應重查共同水力或溫度原因，而不是沿用舊矩陣把新反應自動判成正常。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate correlation from a baseline excluding known anomalies, test seasonal stability and compare instruments using different principles. A changing correlation structure requires examining shared hydraulic or thermal causes rather than automatically classifying new behavior with an outdated covariance model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持兩個殘差大小但反轉其中一個符號，重算聯合距離並比較，提出一項可區分共同基準漂移與相反結構變形的獨立觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep residual magnitudes fixed but reverse one sign, recompute the joint distance and compare. Propose an independent observation that distinguishes common reference drift from opposing structural movements.","failure":"注意干擾：基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用未含已知異常的基線估計相關，檢查不同季節是否穩定，並與不同原理儀器比對。若相關結構本身改變，應重查共同水力或溫度原因，而不是沿用舊矩陣把新反應自動判成正常。","textEn":"Estimate correlation from a baseline excluding known anomalies, test seasonal stability and compare instruments using different principles. A changing correlation structure requires examining shared hydraulic or thermal causes rather than automatically classifying new behavior with an outdated covariance model.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持兩個殘差大小但反轉其中一個符號，重算聯合距離並比較，提出一項可區分共同基準漂移與相反結構變形的獨立觀測。","textEn":"Keep residual magnitudes fixed but reverse one sign, recompute the joint distance and compare. Propose an independent observation that distinguishes common reference drift from opposing structural movements.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「相關監測聯合殘差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Correlated monitoring residuals\"?","options":["用未含已知異常的基線估計相關，檢查不同季節是否穩定，並與不同原理儀器比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","單側位移可以直接當成相鄰接縫開度"],"optionsEn":["Estimate correlation from a baseline excluding known anomalies, test seasonal stability and compare instruments using different principles.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Displacement on one side directly equals the adjacent joint opening."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用未含已知異常的基線估計相關，檢查不同季節是否穩定，並與不同原理儀器比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate correlation from a baseline excluding known anomalies, test seasonal stability and compare instruments using different principles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b207-v15-40","title":"相關監測聯合殘差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Correlated monitoring residuals: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["b207-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「相關監測聯合殘差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Correlated monitoring residuals” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization. A drifting shared reference can also create high correlation between instruments without providing evidence of consistent structural behavior across the monitored locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相關係數接近一時矩陣可能病態，小量測差異會被大幅放大，應檢查基線品質與數值穩定性再解讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A correlation near one makes the covariance matrix ill-conditioned and can amplify small differences; assess baseline quality and numerical stability before interpreting the joint distance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b207-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。","textEn":"Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization. A drifting shared reference can also create high correlation between instruments without providing evidence of consistent structural behavior across the monitored locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"b207-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「相關監測聯合殘差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Correlated monitoring residuals\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。","壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization.","Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-jinping-owner","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
